1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,400
Hook card: most study apps stop at the right answer — this one starts from what you can teach

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:09,500
Dekisugi-kun: middle-school science as a quest map — advance by teaching, not answering

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,800
TEACH BACK node: you explain to Dekisugi-kun — the textbook stays hidden

4
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:17,800
Students teach in their own words — voice or text; never auto-graded or sent

5
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:22,600
On-device check: did your explanation carry the key terms?

6
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:26,600
Miss the key terms and he asks for more — no points lost, just another try

7
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:31,500
Re-reading your own explanation is required first

8
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:38,000
Dekisugi-kun returns one fixed follow-up question from the lesson catalog

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
"Heating created new atoms" — pick the scientifically corrected idea

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:51,000
A miss costs a heart, records the misconception, and triggers a hint — never the answer

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Complete: next node unlocks — fully on-device, no external AI calls

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,500
Optional Plus supporter plan via RevenueCat — paywall: app/lib/screens/plus_screen.dart

13
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:04,000
Profile tab — the karte: a canonical catalog of 29 misconceptions

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
A misconception your explanation corrected flips to 訂正できた — progress is what you taught him
